{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 132, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 1 active, node 2 carries signal, so a conv on edge 5 contributes; otherwise node 2 may be dead."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where none existed helps far more than replacing an existing conv/pool on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Deep conv-heavy cells benefit most from a residual input-output skip."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the residual skip from deep conv cells hurts more than removing a conv on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Node 1 then feeds the output directly, so a conv on edge 0 is actually used."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 is zero and edge 2 carries no signal."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Edge 4 only matters if node 1 receives input from edge 0."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 2 absent, removing edge 1 kills node 2 and the whole 0->2->3 path."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv with pooling loses capacity, whereas replacing a skip costs little."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 absent, removing edge 4 leaves onl